        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          These samplers are portable air quality monitors used for collecting bacterial and fungal specimens from the atmosphere onto a culture medium without impairing their viability.  Air streams entering and exiting the sampler are completely separated, so that turbulence is avoided and air volume can be determined.
<p>
For the first use of microbial air samplers in the Shuttle program, ground-based evaluations of candidate devices were performed.  The devices were required to be small, portable, and battery powered.  Three instruments were the most promising candidates for use in the Shuttle: (1) the Reuter Centrifugal Sampler (RCS), (2) the RCS Plus (Biotest Diagnostics
Corp., Denville, NJ), and (3) the
Burkard air sampler (Burkard Manufacturing Co., Ltd.,Rickmansworth, Hertfordshire, U.K.).  Microbial air samplers were first flown during the Shuttle Extended Duration Orbiter Medical Project (EDOMP) program, and all three devices were assessed in flight.<end></end></p>
